{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And no man.</b> Because Aaron and his sons had ascended with him after the standing at Mount Sinai and descended with them, and he also ascended and stood there the first time." "<b>Throughout the mountain.</b> Even if he is far from the place of the Glory."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The lemma 'ואיש' corresponds to 'ואיש יעלה עמך' in the verse; rendered as 'And no man' per the negative context."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:09.619572512Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}